{
 "_comment": [
  "Routing/DNS profile for v2ray-json subscriptions (YUKU).",
  "Built by MERGING our existing production template with the model used by a",
  "reference RU panel - nothing from our template was dropped.",
  "Rule order matters, Xray takes the first match:",
  " 1. leak checkers (2ip, whoer, browserleaks), yoomoney and Apple stay in the",
  "    tunnel. First on purpose: 2ip.ru is a .ru domain and rule 3 would",
  "    otherwise send it direct, showing the user their real IP.",
  " 2. 17.0.0.0/8 keeps APNs tunnelled so iOS push does not break.",
  " 3. RU + local domains bypass the VPN (banks, gosuslugi, nalog, VK, marketplaces,",
  "    LAN names, reverse-DNS zones).",
  " 4. geoip:private + geoip:ru bypass the VPN. geoip:ru also keeps the Yandex DoH",
  "    resolver and the nalog.ru pins direct - a DoH query through a foreign exit",
  "    returns foreign addresses and the whole scheme collapses.",
  " 5. bittorrent bypasses the VPN (kept from our template).",
  " 6. everything else goes through the tunnel.",
  "domainStrategy is IPIfNonMatch, not AsIs: under AsIs an unmatched domain is",
  "never resolved locally, so geoip rules would almost never fire.",
  "Ad/telemetry blocking was available in the reference panel and NOT taken.",
  "Invisible U+2060 characters were stripped from two Apple entries copied out of",
  "our template, where they silently prevented the rule from matching.",
  "Requires geoip.dat on the client (Happ, v2rayNG and Streisand ship it)."
 ],
